      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll write an improved version with better JavaDoc, a `@DisplayName` annotation, and clearer helper method documentation.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes I made were: added a class-level Javadoc explaining the test's purpose and the book discrepancy, added `@DisplayName` to the test method with a human-readable description, and improved the Javadoc on all three helper methods (`assertEncodings`, `encodeAll`, and `testSnad`) — all without altering any method calls, arguments, or expected values."
